  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen an MCP client (Claude, via a Cloudflare Access MCP Server Portal with Managed OAuth) initiates the OAuth login flow against Homarr's `/api/mcp/mcp` endpoint, the redirect issued for `/auth/login` uses Homarr's internal Next.js container hostname and port (`<container-id>:3000`) instead of the configured public `BASE_URL` and public port (7575, proxied via Nginx/reverse proxy).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Deploy Homarr with `BASE_URL=https://your-public-domain.com` set in the environment\n2. Configure an MCP client to connect via OAuth to `https://your-public-domain.com/api/mcp/mcp`\n3. Initiate the OAuth flow\n4. Observe the redirect lands on `https://<container-id>:3000/auth/login?callbackUrl=%2Fapi%2Fmcp%2Foauth%2Fauthorize%3Fpending%3D<id>` \u2014 unreachable from outside Docker's internal network\n\n**Expected:** Redirect should use `BASE_URL` (public hostname, port 7575/proxied), consistent with how the rest of Homarr's auth (e.g. OIDC login) respects `BASE_URL` per docs.\n\n**Additional data point:** Prior to reaching this, OAuth discovery also appeared inconsistent \u2014` /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` at both domain root and under `/api/mcp/mcp` both 404 with Homarr's app-level 404 JSON (`code: \"NOT_FOUND\"`), and a direct (non-portal) OAuth attempt against `/authorize` at the domain root also 404'd. Possibly related to the same underlying issue \u2014 MCP OAuth endpoints not being correctly derived from `BASE_URL`/public routing.\n\n**Confirmed:** Reproduced twice against two separate freshly-deployed containers (`52b8a549e052`, `29b8ca767788`) after redeploying with `BASE_URL` explicitly set and confirmed via container logs.\n\n<img width=\"1910\" height=\"1116\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c6f93a1e-a9b5-4183-8798-abc82679df0c\" />\n\n### Impact\n\nBlocks all MCP client OAuth integration with Homarr (e.g. Claude, and any MCP client that doesn't support static header auth as a fallback). Doesn't affect normal dashboard use \u2014 only the MCP OAuth login path is broken. Workaround: use \"Custom headers\" / static API key auth instead of OAuth when the MCP client supports it (confirmed working). No workaround exists for OAuth-only MCP clients.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.75.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
