      "updated_at": "2026-08-19T08:24:16Z",
      "body": "Fixed in #6631. Two root causes:\n\n1. **Login redirect used the internal container origin** \u2014 `/api/mcp/oauth/authorize` built the redirect to `/auth/login` from `url.origin`, which is `<container-id>:3000` inside Docker. It now derives the base URL from the request headers (`x-forwarded-proto`/`x-forwarded-host`, falling back to `host`) \u2014 the same mechanism the rest of Homarr's auth and the OIDC flow use behind a reverse proxy.\n\n2. **`/.well-known/oauth-*` returned 404** \u2014 Next.js's App Router doesn't route dot-prefixed folders, so the OAuth discovery endpoints never existed at the public URLs. They're now served via rewrites at `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`, `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`, and the RFC 8414 path-prefixed location under `/api/mcp/:transport/\u2026` (what Cloudflare Access MCP Server Portal requests).\n\nNo env vars or public URLs changed, so no configuration changes are required. Once the CI image is green, redeploying should unblock OAuth-based MCP clients (Claude, portal-managed OAuth, etc.).",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
