      "created_at": "2026-08-22T20:06:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-22T20:06:43Z",
      "body": "That's the right fix. Pinning the issuer and redirects to a configured `BASE_URL` keeps RFC 8414 \u00a73.3 satisfied no matter what a proxy in front does with `Host` or `x-forwarded-*`, and the header fallback covers the case where it's unset.\n\nOnce #6631 merges I'll stand up a homarr instance behind a reverse proxy and run `npx mcpcomp` against it to confirm the issuer holds end to end. I can also contribute a homarr fixture plus a small CI check that fails the build if the advertised issuer ever comes from a request header, so this can't quietly come back. Want me to open that?\n\n(mcpcomp is the scanner from the earlier comment.)\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
