      "created_at": "2026-08-22T20:15:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-22T20:15:13Z",
      "body": "Ran it against `https://demo.homarr.dev/api/mcp/mcp`. Grade C, one requirement violation, and the good news first: the discovery problem from this issue is gone on the demo. The `.well-known` documents serve 200 and the challenge points `resource_metadata` at `https://demo.homarr.dev/...`, the public domain, not an internal container origin. So the BASE_URL fix is doing its job here.\n\nThe one graded finding is a different, smaller one on the token-expiry path:\n\nThe 401 for a *rejected* token carries no `WWW-Authenticate` header. The no-credential 401 does carry it, but when a client presents an invalid or expired token, the 401 comes back bare. OAuth 2.1 \u00a75.3.1 wants the challenge on that response too, because a client whose token just expired re-discovers the auth server from it. Without the header it falls back to guessing the well-known URIs, which still work here, so it's medium not critical.\n\nRepro (the demo rate-limits repeated probes with 429, so space these out):\n\n```bash\n# no credential: 401 WITH the challenge\ncurl -sD - -o /dev/null -X POST https://demo.homarr.dev/api/mcp/mcp \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' -H 'accept: application/json, text/event-stream' \\\n  -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{}}' | grep -i www-authenticate\n\n# invalid token: 401 WITHOUT the challenge\ncurl -sD - -o /dev/null -X POST https://demo.homarr.dev/api/mcp/mcp \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' -H 'accept: application/json, text/event-stream' \\\n  -H 'authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token' \\\n  -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{}}' | grep -i www-authenticate\n```\n\nFix is to send the same `WWW-Authenticate` header on the rejected-token 401 that the credential-less one already emits.\n\nTwo advisories that don't affect the grade, if you're tidying up: the AS advertises a `registration_endpoint` but no Client ID Metadata Documents (DCR is deprecated as of 2026-07-28), and `authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported` (RFC 9207) isn't advertised.\n\nHappy to send the full report. And the offer still stands to add a homarr fixture plus a CI check so the discovery regression this issue was about can't come back silently.\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
