      "updated_at": "2026-08-27T03:00:01Z",
      "body": "> Can you try the `ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr-test:pr-6631` docker image and let me know if it fixes your issue [@SoloStarship](https://github.com/SoloStarship) ? The message above was an LLM yapping, sorry about that.\n\nHi Dev,\n\nThe fix seemed to work perfectly.\n\n**Verified PR #6631 fixes both issues from #6628, tested against `ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr-test:pr-6631`**\n\nDeployed the test image on a separate amd64 host (my production Homarr runs on arm64, and this test tag is amd64-only \u2014 confirmed via `docker manifest inspect`, single-platform manifest, no arm64 variant), with `BASE_URL` set to the container's own reachable LAN address.\n\n1. **Well-known discovery** \u2014 `GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` now returns valid metadata JSON, with every URL (`authorization_endpoint, token_endpoint, registration_endpoint`) correctly derived from `BASE_URL` rather than 404ing. Confirms the second bug (dot-prefixed folder routing) is fixed.\n2. **Dynamic client registration** \u2014 `POST /api/mcp/oauth/register` with a standard DCR payload returned a valid `client_id/client_secret` pair.\n3. **Full authorize redirect chain** \u2014 navigated the browser directly to `/api/mcp/oauth/authorize` with the registered `client_id` and a placeholder `redirect_uri` of `http://localhost/callback`. The browser followed the entire redirect chain (login/consent \u2192 callback) and landed on` http://localhost/callback?code=<valid-auth-code>` \u2014 meaning every hop in between resolved on a real, externally-reachable hostname. Pre-fix, this chain broke immediately at the first redirect to an unreachable `<container-id>:3000` address. Confirms the first bug (login redirect using internal origin instead of `BASE_URL`) is fixed.\n\n**What I'm waiting on**: PR #6631 to get an approving review and merge, then a new multi-arch (amd64+arm64) `homarr-labs/homarr:latest` image published \u2014 my production instance runs on arm64 (Raspberry Pi), so this amd64-only test build can't go there. Once that ships I'll redeploy production and retry the actual Claude MCP connector OAuth flow end-to-end through my Cloudflare Access portal.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
